          "name": "Grafana Remove Provider Settings",
          "request": {
            "name": "Grafana Remove Provider Settings",
            "description": {
              "content": "This API operation allows you to delete a specific single sign-on (SSO) provider configuration from Grafana by specifying the provider's unique key in the URL path. When executed, it removes all settings and configuration associated with that particular SSO provider, effectively disabling that authentication method for your Grafana instance. This is useful when you need to decommission an SSO integration, clean up unused authentication providers, or reconfigure your authentication setup from scratch. The operation requires the provider key identifier to target the specific SSO configuration you want to remove, and upon successful deletion, the provider will no longer be available as an authentication option for users.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
